      "description": "Build Your Career at Columbia College | Columbia College Skip to main content Toggle menu Degrees & Programs Degrees & Programs All Degrees + Certificates (Program Finder) Columbia College Global Schools Academic Calendar Academic Resources Catalog Your Path To Success Discover more than 20 new academic programs online, designed to meet the needs of tomorrow’s workforce. learn more Admissions Admissions Why Columbia College? Partnerships How to Apply Admitted Students How to Transfer Refer a Student Visit Dedicated Support You're building your future, and we are here to guide you every step of the way. contact admissions Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Affordability at Columbia College How To Apply For Aid Tuition & Cost of Attendance Scholarships Military Affiliated Benefits Frequently Asked Questions FAFSA Apply online through the free application. Columbia College's school code is 002456. view the fafsa process Student Life Student Life Living on Campus Support & Services Organizations & Societies Bookstore High School To College Transition Events Calendar Commencement You Are Welcome Here Our campus is more than a location, it's a community. A place where everyone belongs, where everyone is welcome. view campus map Athletics about about Who We Are Leadership Accreditation Board of Trustees Awards Strategic Plan State Regulatory Information A Legacy of Excellence For 175+ years, our life-changing educational experiences, and safe and welcoming environment make it possible for every student to truly thrive. view our mission, vision & values Current Students Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni Request Info Visit Apply Give Toggle search search Search Search popular searches Admission requirements Financial Aid deadlines Tuition Faculty directory Course schedule Study abroad Advising Online resources Student Success Coaches Admissions Dates & Deadlines Transcripts Columbia College Columbia College Request Info Visit Apply Give Build Your Career at Columbia College Cultivating Talent, Nurturing Growth At Columbia College, our Human Resources department is dedicated to empowering the college's most significant resources – its employees. Job Opportunities Benefits Guide Employee Policies 2025 1095C’s If you are wanting to request your 2025 1095C, please contact humanresources@ccis.edu . If you are a current employee, you can login to MyPortal, go to Employee Self Service and find your 1095C under the Tax Information area. If you have any questions or need assistance please reach out to the Human Resources Office. Employee Benefits Retirement Plan With us, your future is in good hands. We offer a generous retirement plan to our staff, matching up to 6% after meeting eligibility requirements. It's our way of ensuring that you can look forward to a secure and comfortable retirement. Health & Wellness We believe in the power of rest and rejuvenation. That's why we offer our employees a generous amount of vacation and sick leave, comprehensive health, dental, vision, and life insurance options, along with an around-the-clock Employee Assistance Program. Education Benefits As a firm believer in lifelong learning, we offer free and discounted tuition for employees and their dependents, as well as countless professional development opportunities, and access to 13,000+ LinkedIn Learning courses. Your progress is our mission. Employee Perks With 24/7 campus safety, free parking, fitness center access, Microsoft Office, and entry to home athletic events for you and five guests, we're saying 'thanks'. You are essential to our visionary community. Why Work At Columbia College? At Columbia College, we strive to create an inclusive employee experience for everyone, regardless of race, color, national origin, gender, religion, sexual orientation, age, or disability. Columbia College is a safe place for open dialogue, a supporter of activities promoting diversity and inclusion, and ultimately, a community that welcomes all. Equal Opportunity Employment As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Columbia College ensures that qualified applicants are considered for positions without discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, nationality, ethnicity, age, sexual orientation, marital or veteran status, the presence of a non-job-related medical condition or disability, or any other legally protected status. In compliance with the Clery Act, the College discloses crime statistics for crimes committed on campus, in certain off-campus buildings, or on property owned/controlled by the College during the last three years. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be obtained electronically or in paper copy by contacting the Campus Safety Office. because a future built by you is a future built for you. Too many people have been made to feel that higher education isn’t a place for them — that it is someone else’s dream. But we change all that. With individualized attention and ongoing support, we help you write a new story for the future where you play the starring role. request info visit campus apply register for classes Columbia College 1001 Rogers Street, Columbia, MO 65216 (573) 875-8700 contact us YouTube Instagram Facebook Twitter LinkedIn TikTok About Careers News Calendar Directory Locations & Maps Safety & Emergencies Submit Your Deposit myPortal Log In Accessibility Resources Title IX Policies Privacy Policy Consumer Information Back to Top State Regulatory Information Public Disclosures and Licensure State Authorization Reciprocity Agreement Complaint Process California Performance Fact Sheets © 2026 Columbia College"
